    DIGITAL Expands Its Relationship with NCI to Deliver Worldwide Systems 
        Integration Services for Network Computer Deployments


MAYNARD, Mass., April 14, 1997 - Digital Equipment Corporation today
announced that it has been designated by Network Computers. Inc., 
(NCI) a wholly owned subsidiary of Oracle Corporation,  as a 
Preferred Systems Integration Provider. The company also announced 
the availability of NCI's network computer server software on 
Digital's family of 64-bit AlphaServer systems. 

     Today's announcement results from an extensive collaboration 
between NCI and Digital to provide a total enterprise-wide network 
computer solution for NCI's customers. The announcement comes on the 
heels of Digital's recent joint introduction with NCI of the DIGITAL 
Network Appliance Reference Design initiative.  As a result of this 
expanded partnership, Digital will provide NCI's customers with a 
network-based solution comprising end-to-end product and services.  
Included are Digital's AlphaServer 64-bit family of systems and a 
suite of life cycle service and support programs for planning, 
designing, implementing, supporting and maintaining network
computers systems incorporating NCI's server software products 
across an enterprise network.

     NCI's server products include NC Server and NC Enterprise 
server software. NC Server is a complete, packaged, low 
administration offering for schools, local governments and corporate 
workgroups. It includes NCOS -- NCI's low cost operating system, 
personal productivity applications, networking software, and all key 
services for managing and administering network computers. NC 
Enterprise is a highly scalable system that provides corporations 
with all the services needed for the management of network 
computers, such as initialization, support for printing and file 
sharing, and server and application management functions. 

     As a Preferred Systems Integration Provider, Digital will have 
a worldwide role in helping global enterprises move to a network 
computer system incorporating NCI's server software. Digital will 
draw on its highly trained service professionals in over 100 
countries and its years of experience designing and implementing 
local and wide-area networks. Initial service offerings will 
facilitate the integration of NCs and Digital AlphaServers running 
NC Server software into the enterprise computing environment.
The service offerings include:

Network Architecture Consulting

     o  Simulation and Modeling

     o  Logical and Physical Network Design

     o  Systems and Network Management Design

     o  NC Implementation Services


     "Digital and NCI have combined their unique strengths to 
deliver a comprehensive solution set to customers," said Kannankote 
Srikanth, vice president and general manager, Digital Network and 
Systems Integration Services. "NCI is a proven leader in developing 
software for the network computing environment, and their collaboration 
with Digital will allow customers to take full advantage of it's extensive 
experience designing and implementing networked business solutions and the 
superior scalability, reliability and cost-effectiveness found in 
Digital's high-performance AlphaServer line."  

     "Known for their high levels of service and support, Digital 
uniquely offers a complete solution for our NC customers," said 
Jerry Baker, CEO of NCI. "From a high performance StrongARM 
reference profile to scalable AlphaServers, the combination of our 
technology with Digital services provides an excellent platform 
deploying today's network computing solutions." 

     Digital's AlphaServers provide the most powerful and scalable 
platform available for the processing-intensive environment required 
for NC servers.  They are the industry's only complete line of 
high-performance 64-bit RISC servers.  

     NCI, a wholly-owned subsidiary of Oracle Corporation, develops,
licenses and markets all software, technology and support services 
for the network computer, including NC Access, NC Enterprise and NC 
Card.  With strategic alliances worldwide, NCI's mission is to bring 
network computing to the corporate, consumer and educational 
marketplaces. NCI's World Wide Web address is http://www.nc.com  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's scalable Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.  
